  "about": [
    "Degree table for toDegree: every spelled root (and bass) in all 12 keys, Roman style.",
    "Derived from the Degree calculation rule in the chord-conversion spec, independently of the code:",
    "a note on the major scale of the tonic is the plain degree whatever its spelling; off the scale,",
    "a sharp spelling is # of the degree below, a flat spelling is b of the degree above, and a",
    "natural spelling is one of bII, bIII, #IV, bVI, bVII.",
    "`tonic` is the pitch class (C = 0). The same row serves the major and the minor key on that tonic."
